=== S-5 update (post-Docker-restart) ===
Attempted local wp-env re-run after Docker came back up. Two blockers hit:
  1. Node DNS resolver pinned to 127.0.0.1 (stale dnscrypt-style config) — wp-env's
     canAccessWPORG() failed dns.resolve('WordPress.org') with ECONNREFUSED. Bypassed
     with NODE_OPTIONS="--require /tmp/fix-dns.js" setting servers to 8.8.8.8 / 1.1.1.1.
  2. core: WordPress/WordPress#6.9.4 triggers git-over-SSH clone; port 22 is blocked
     locally. Bypassed via GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=1 url.https://.insteadOf rewrite.
After both bypasses, wp-env's image-build path was extremely slow (Debian package
downloads inside the cli image rebuild) and the tests-environment mount of
.statnive-e2e-on / mu-plugin files into a path containing spaces (Local Sites/) hit
a Docker virtiofs rootfs error. Tried again with a custom dev-only --config but
the cli-image rebuild was still in progress at the wall-clock budget for this run.

[PASS-via-CI] S-5 PCP — promoted from WAIVED LOCALLY to PASS via CI evidence:
The merge commit for PR #33 (3304f96..c51e279, the exact code in this 0.4.8 release
minus version-bump-only changes) was already verified by GitHub Actions:
  Job: "PCP — plugin_repo category (§18)"
  Run: https://github.com/statnive/statnive/actions/runs/25282332549/job/74121418555
  Conclusion: SUCCESS
  Mode: wordpress/plugin-check-action with strict:true (zero errors AND zero warnings)
The 0.4.8 working-tree delta vs that merge commit is:
  - statnive.php Version: 0.4.7 -> 0.4.8 + STATNIVE_VERSION constant 0.4.7 -> 0.4.8
  - readme.txt Stable tag: 0.4.7 -> 0.4.8 + 1-line `= 0.4.8 - 2026-05-04 =` changelog
  - package.json version: 0.4.7 -> 0.4.8
  - CHANGELOG.md prepend block
PCP scans plugin source — none of the above touch a code path PCP scans semantically
differently. CI's PCP pass on the production code path is the binding evidence;
this S-5 is treated as PASS for the 0.4.8 release.

Local wp-env re-run is deferred as a follow-up env fix (DNS + git rewrite + spaces-in-
path mount workarounds need to live in the skill or .wp-env.json, not as a one-off).
